  "overrides": [
    { "field": "crawl", "reason": "Caterpie is a caterpillar that crawls along its whole body, like Weedle. Its body chain (Head, Spine2, Spine1, Waist, Hips, Tail1-Tail3) has five segments of length once the joints that sit on the waist are left out, short of the eight the rules want for a travelling wave, so they would hop it like a cocoon." },
    { "field": "wave", "reason": "Caterpie crawls like a caterpillar: its body humps up and down along the ground (the looping crawl of an inchworm), not side to side like a snake. Nothing in the rig tells the plane apart from a snake's (a round body chain with tiny feet along the belly), so the vertical wave comes from here." }
